WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.070 --> 00:00:02.240
- [Mark] All right, Patrick.

00:00:02.240 --> 00:00:03.630
Welcome back.

00:00:03.630 --> 00:00:04.463
- Thanks for having me.

00:00:04.463 --> 00:00:06.915
- [Mark] Yeah, so your last talk

00:00:06.915 --> 00:00:10.104
was a very interesting
one because you were

00:00:10.104 --> 00:00:11.550
thick in the middle

00:00:11.550 --> 00:00:13.790
of a like a week long binge right?

00:00:13.790 --> 00:00:15.500
- [Patrick] Yeah, Yeah, I watched it.

00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:16.443
I was very high.

00:00:17.280 --> 00:00:18.113
- [Mark] Yes you were.

00:00:18.113 --> 00:00:21.020
And I thought now would be
a good time to bring you in

00:00:21.020 --> 00:00:23.780
'cause now you're clean and sober.

00:00:23.780 --> 00:00:26.240
- Clean and sober at the moment,
yeah, it's been a few days

00:00:26.240 --> 00:00:27.330
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:00:27.330 --> 00:00:28.920
- Since I have been able to get high.

00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:30.575
- [Mark] And have you lost your job?

00:00:30.575 --> 00:00:31.527
- No.

00:00:31.527 --> 00:00:32.478
- [Mark] That's the number one question

00:00:32.478 --> 00:00:33.428
everyone's gonna ask you
if you lost your job.

00:00:33.428 --> 00:00:34.640
- I haven't lost my job,
I need to, you know,

00:00:34.640 --> 00:00:37.060
I need to be responsible
and I need to go to rehab.

00:00:37.060 --> 00:00:39.730
I will wind up in rehab soon

00:00:39.730 --> 00:00:41.500
and then we'll see what
happens with the job.

00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:44.070
I honestly don't care about the job

00:00:44.070 --> 00:00:48.223
as much as like my life, you know?

00:00:49.550 --> 00:00:51.770
The depression and the...

00:00:54.580 --> 00:00:56.690
just the overwhelmingness of this thing

00:00:56.690 --> 00:01:01.420
that happens to me that I do is so heavy.

00:01:01.420 --> 00:01:02.570
You know, It's so heavy

00:01:04.002 --> 00:01:05.420
and there's a lot of
guilt and a lot of shame,

00:01:05.420 --> 00:01:07.733
you know, like the idea
of going back to work

00:01:07.733 --> 00:01:10.760
and seeing all my people
is hard right now.

00:01:10.760 --> 00:01:11.956
- [Mark] Right.

00:01:11.956 --> 00:01:12.905
- At this point.

00:01:12.905 --> 00:01:13.738
- [Mark] How have you not lost your job?

00:01:13.738 --> 00:01:16.067
Because most jobs you'd be fired by now?

00:01:16.067 --> 00:01:19.930
- I think the environment
these days is it's...

00:01:19.930 --> 00:01:21.340
- [Mark] Did they know
that you had this problem?

00:01:21.340 --> 00:01:22.173
- Yeah, they do.

00:01:22.173 --> 00:01:24.337
- [Mark] Oh, so they
kind of work with you?

00:01:24.337 --> 00:01:25.570
- I mean they want to help me.

00:01:25.570 --> 00:01:27.007
They love me.

00:01:27.007 --> 00:01:28.500
I love them.

00:01:28.500 --> 00:01:31.920
And you know, its like, it's a disease

00:01:31.920 --> 00:01:34.277
and it's like a medical disease.

00:01:34.277 --> 00:01:36.910
And I always do, like, my best.

00:01:36.910 --> 00:01:39.313
Like I use all my effort
to try to stay clean.

00:01:40.300 --> 00:01:41.133
So I don't know.

00:01:41.133 --> 00:01:41.966
I mean, I haven't really spoken

00:01:41.966 --> 00:01:44.020
to any of the managers directly about it.

00:01:44.020 --> 00:01:46.970
But they just want what's best for me

00:01:46.970 --> 00:01:49.970
and right now what's best
for me is to get help.

00:01:49.970 --> 00:01:53.733
And what happens with the
job, it comes down the road.

00:01:54.630 --> 00:01:57.640
But I don't think it's as common

00:01:57.640 --> 00:01:59.780
as it used to be in the
past to just fire people

00:01:59.780 --> 00:02:02.570
especially if they're honest
about what's going on.

00:02:02.570 --> 00:02:03.403
So...

00:02:03.403 --> 00:02:05.300
- [Mark] And you certainly were honest.

00:02:05.300 --> 00:02:07.473
- Yeah. I mean, I was.

00:02:07.473 --> 00:02:08.710
Like some of this stuff I said

00:02:08.710 --> 00:02:10.553
on there was wow, what the hell?

00:02:11.495 --> 00:02:13.617
But it's the truth. That's all.

00:02:14.487 --> 00:02:17.173
- [Mark] I mean, what do you think,

00:02:18.090 --> 00:02:21.240
I mean, certainly crack
is an addictive substance

00:02:21.240 --> 00:02:24.500
but I like to go to the
deeper levels of things

00:02:24.500 --> 00:02:26.423
and just to figure out what the core,

00:02:27.570 --> 00:02:29.080
the stem of it is, the cause of it.

00:02:29.080 --> 00:02:32.030
And is there something

00:02:34.100 --> 00:02:35.180
in your self-worth

00:02:35.180 --> 00:02:38.840
or something that maybe
is blocking you from.

00:02:38.840 --> 00:02:41.440
I kinda see you're intelligent clearly,

00:02:41.440 --> 00:02:42.900
and you could...

00:02:43.920 --> 00:02:45.853
You must see that this,

00:02:47.240 --> 00:02:50.100
if you do this again it'll
lead to more self-destruction.

00:02:50.100 --> 00:02:51.050
Eventually you'll be homeless,

00:02:51.050 --> 00:02:52.450
losing your employment.

00:02:52.450 --> 00:02:53.669
- Yeah.

00:02:53.669 --> 00:02:54.530
- [Mark] Losing your
income and everything,

00:02:54.530 --> 00:02:56.360
and you'll lose your teeth

00:02:56.360 --> 00:02:57.230
and you'll lose everything

00:02:57.230 --> 00:02:59.832
and maybe your life even.

00:02:59.832 --> 00:03:00.783
- Right.

00:03:00.783 --> 00:03:02.730
- [Mark] And you're intelligent
enough to know that,

00:03:02.730 --> 00:03:05.140
but yet you still repeat this behavior.

00:03:05.140 --> 00:03:07.800
- Right. That's what makes
it super frustrating,

00:03:07.800 --> 00:03:09.300
even more frustrating than I told...

00:03:09.300 --> 00:03:11.730
I absolutely know what's gonna happen.

00:03:11.730 --> 00:03:14.887
And eventually I always
wind up doing it anyway.

00:03:14.887 --> 00:03:16.990
And that to me, that's
sort of like the definition

00:03:16.990 --> 00:03:18.540
of the disease of addiction.

00:03:18.540 --> 00:03:20.090
Is that knowing what's going to happen

00:03:20.090 --> 00:03:23.420
and it's one thing to be
high and then you can't stop.

00:03:23.420 --> 00:03:24.470
You can't stop And then eventually

00:03:24.470 --> 00:03:25.640
the drugs get out of your system

00:03:25.640 --> 00:03:27.680
and you're sober for a few days.

00:03:27.680 --> 00:03:32.650
And then the brain
insists on doing it again.

00:03:32.650 --> 00:03:33.840
Insists on doing it again,

00:03:33.840 --> 00:03:36.820
even knowing you're
gonna destroy everything.

00:03:36.820 --> 00:03:40.065
Just I don't care. I want that feeling.

00:03:40.065 --> 00:03:41.520
- [Mark] And intelligence and common sense

00:03:41.520 --> 00:03:42.770
won't factor in, right?

00:03:42.770 --> 00:03:44.332
- It doesn't factor in

00:03:44.332 --> 00:03:47.400
- [Mark] Does like reducing
stress or getting rest

00:03:47.400 --> 00:03:48.960
or sleep or anything like that?

00:03:48.960 --> 00:03:50.807
- All those things do help.

00:03:50.807 --> 00:03:53.420
That those all these sort of
like recovery type things,

00:03:53.420 --> 00:03:57.010
which I do, like I said, I do that.

00:03:57.010 --> 00:04:00.490
The 12 steps, meditation, exercise.

00:04:00.490 --> 00:04:04.083
Like healthy living, you know.

00:04:04.083 --> 00:04:06.090
Going after like goals.

00:04:06.090 --> 00:04:07.060
I go after all these goals,

00:04:07.060 --> 00:04:09.580
but I never get there because
I'm always on another relapse.

00:04:09.580 --> 00:04:11.777
And then the relapse
is a destructive thing.

00:04:11.777 --> 00:04:12.728
- [Mark] Right.

00:04:12.728 --> 00:04:14.350
- And it takes a couple months to at least

00:04:14.350 --> 00:04:18.692
to even get back to point
zero and start again.

00:04:18.692 --> 00:04:23.520
So yeah, I mean, and the thing
is I kind of hold onto hope.

00:04:23.520 --> 00:04:26.547
You know, like I hold onto
hope that this might work now.

00:04:26.547 --> 00:04:29.084
You know, like, it might work now.

00:04:29.084 --> 00:04:32.120
And God might take away

00:04:32.120 --> 00:04:34.480
that broken thing in my brain, you know.

00:04:34.480 --> 00:04:35.990
Like the part of my brain

00:04:35.990 --> 00:04:37.670
that knowing what's gonna
happen, does it anyway,

00:04:37.670 --> 00:04:39.730
that instead of me having
to fight against that.

00:04:39.730 --> 00:04:42.800
Because the fight, it's never successful.

00:04:42.800 --> 00:04:45.470
It might be successful
on like one or two times,

00:04:45.470 --> 00:04:46.303
like, I really wanna do it,

00:04:46.303 --> 00:04:47.520
Ah, I'm not gonna do it.

00:04:47.520 --> 00:04:49.400
But eventually, it fails.

00:04:49.400 --> 00:04:51.370
My own strength always fails.

00:04:51.370 --> 00:04:52.500
That's what, like, the idea is

00:04:52.500 --> 00:04:54.815
that possibly God will
remove it right off the...

00:04:54.815 --> 00:04:56.010
- [Mark] Like a lobotomy?

00:04:56.010 --> 00:04:57.500
- Yeah. Like, instead of it coming,

00:04:57.500 --> 00:04:58.970
and I fight it and I succeed,

00:04:58.970 --> 00:05:00.130
it doesn't come.

00:05:00.130 --> 00:05:01.750
That's like the idea of like the 12 steps.

00:05:01.750 --> 00:05:02.960
- [Mark] The part of your
brain that triggers it.

00:05:02.960 --> 00:05:05.528
- Yeah, that gets removed by
something other than myself.

00:05:05.528 --> 00:05:06.361
- [Mark] Right.

00:05:06.361 --> 00:05:07.707
- Right, because like,
what's the quote, like

00:05:07.707 --> 00:05:09.777
"I can't solve the problem..."

00:05:09.777 --> 00:05:11.730
"The same brain that cause a problem,

00:05:11.730 --> 00:05:12.660
can't solve the problem."

00:05:12.660 --> 00:05:14.660
I think that's an Einstein quote.

00:05:14.660 --> 00:05:16.043
And that's what we try to do.

00:05:16.043 --> 00:05:17.763
I try to use my crack head brain

00:05:17.763 --> 00:05:20.050
to solve my crack head problem.

00:05:20.050 --> 00:05:22.250
- [Mark] Yeah, and then
the 12 steps kind of...

00:05:22.250 --> 00:05:25.180
- It was designed to
get you into a position

00:05:25.180 --> 00:05:27.830
where a god will remove it,

00:05:27.830 --> 00:05:29.920
will remove the obsession, they call it.

00:05:29.920 --> 00:05:32.950
And I was doing that, you
know, I was doing that.

00:05:32.950 --> 00:05:34.700
I was making amends on my nine-step,

00:05:34.700 --> 00:05:36.060
which is another kind
of embarrassing thing.

00:05:36.060 --> 00:05:37.740
I was going around making, you know,

00:05:37.740 --> 00:05:39.730
sort of like apologizing to people

00:05:39.730 --> 00:05:44.074
and having like really deep sort of like

00:05:44.074 --> 00:05:46.760
beautiful conversations
with people, you know,

00:05:46.760 --> 00:05:47.780
that really want the best for me

00:05:47.780 --> 00:05:48.870
and be very honest with them.

00:05:48.870 --> 00:05:50.910
Like I, like you, could imagine.

00:05:50.910 --> 00:05:53.252
And, you know, just a couple of weeks ago,

00:05:53.252 --> 00:05:55.203
three, four weeks ago I was doing that.

00:05:56.335 --> 00:05:58.680
And here I am, you
know, so it's hard, man.

00:05:58.680 --> 00:06:02.010
It's very, very depressing, you know?

00:06:02.010 --> 00:06:02.993
Very depressing.

00:06:04.200 --> 00:06:05.900
- [Mark] And you've been
through rehab before?

00:06:05.900 --> 00:06:07.030
- Yeah, probably 20 times

00:06:07.030 --> 00:06:07.930
- [Mark] 20 times.

00:06:10.320 --> 00:06:13.370
I wish there was some
solution to this problem.

00:06:13.370 --> 00:06:15.439
- Yeah, no, I talked to my dad and he's,

00:06:15.439 --> 00:06:18.470
he just, I could tell he just feels so bad

00:06:18.470 --> 00:06:21.921
that I have to, like, I
have to have this, you know?

00:06:21.921 --> 00:06:24.940
'Cause he says like what
you were saying from,

00:06:24.940 --> 00:06:27.554
he says it, he knows me
better than anyone like that.

00:06:27.554 --> 00:06:28.949
I have...

00:06:28.949 --> 00:06:31.730
I'm great, like, in all the other ways,

00:06:31.730 --> 00:06:32.770
like, people love me.

00:06:32.770 --> 00:06:33.603
I do good.

00:06:33.603 --> 00:06:34.893
I try hard.

00:06:34.893 --> 00:06:35.726
I'm nice.

00:06:36.604 --> 00:06:37.590
And it's just one thing,

00:06:37.590 --> 00:06:40.520
it's this one crippling thing that has now

00:06:40.520 --> 00:06:44.440
is like just like a
lifelong anchor and like,

00:06:44.440 --> 00:06:47.294
damn it, why did I have
to get this, you know?

00:06:47.294 --> 00:06:48.700
- [Mark] Yeah, 'cause
clearly you're a good guy.

00:06:48.700 --> 00:06:49.778
You're intelligent.

00:06:49.778 --> 00:06:52.019
You have all these great qualities.

00:06:52.019 --> 00:06:53.797
- That would have been great.

00:06:53.797 --> 00:06:55.300
Why did this have to stick to me?

00:06:55.300 --> 00:06:56.516
I don't know.

00:06:56.516 --> 00:06:58.473
You know, he feels bad,

00:06:58.473 --> 00:06:59.306
people feel bad,

00:06:59.306 --> 00:07:00.163
people want to help.

00:07:02.960 --> 00:07:05.387
You know, especially
once I do this, you know,

00:07:05.387 --> 00:07:08.010
and I'm like sort of in
the aftermath part of it

00:07:08.010 --> 00:07:11.210
kinda like right now, I'm so depressed.

00:07:11.210 --> 00:07:13.830
Most of the time that I can't
even got to get off the couch.

00:07:13.830 --> 00:07:16.498
- [Mark] So I think I may
have asked this last time,

00:07:16.498 --> 00:07:21.498
is this a genetic thing or
is it a self-worth thing?

00:07:21.510 --> 00:07:22.720
- I mean, self-worth, probably.

00:07:22.720 --> 00:07:23.553
I don't know about genetic.

00:07:23.553 --> 00:07:24.520
I guess it is genetics.

00:07:24.520 --> 00:07:28.580
You know, like it definitely
runs in my family.

00:07:28.580 --> 00:07:32.573
Not my parents, but my, you
know, brothers and cousins.

00:07:32.573 --> 00:07:34.390
Yeah, self-worth.

00:07:34.390 --> 00:07:35.950
My self-worth is zero.

00:07:35.950 --> 00:07:37.680
And I was thinking about this recently,

00:07:37.680 --> 00:07:39.220
talking to somebody, too, like,

00:07:39.220 --> 00:07:40.380
even in between, you know,

00:07:40.380 --> 00:07:43.530
like I'll be clean, doing
good, doing 12 steps,

00:07:43.530 --> 00:07:45.390
doing my life, going to work, enjoy it.

00:07:45.390 --> 00:07:47.350
I'm always, I'm always happy.

00:07:47.350 --> 00:07:48.183
I'm always happy.

00:07:48.183 --> 00:07:51.410
Like, I'm always like, like
in the moment, like content,

00:07:51.410 --> 00:07:53.550
but my self-worth is very low.

00:07:53.550 --> 00:07:55.290
- [Mark] Yeah, I go to
a gym every morning.

00:07:55.290 --> 00:07:56.720
I do it every day of the year.

00:07:56.720 --> 00:07:58.640
And this morning I was there

00:07:58.640 --> 00:07:59.820
early in the morning, it's raining.

00:07:59.820 --> 00:08:01.667
I have to do it outdoors because of COVID

00:08:01.667 --> 00:08:03.270
and it's pouring rain and I'm working out

00:08:03.270 --> 00:08:05.680
in the rain with just, you
know, it's freezing cold

00:08:05.680 --> 00:08:07.187
and there's a bunch of
other people doing it.

00:08:07.187 --> 00:08:08.490
And I was joking with somebody

00:08:08.490 --> 00:08:10.360
that the only the reason these people

00:08:10.360 --> 00:08:15.360
are so dedicated is most, I would bet you,

00:08:15.400 --> 00:08:17.809
half of them have addiction issues.

00:08:17.809 --> 00:08:20.670
And they've replaced that
addiction with exercise.

00:08:20.670 --> 00:08:22.414
- I was at the gym all the time

00:08:22.414 --> 00:08:26.370
and I haven't been since COVID
originally hit, but yeah.

00:08:26.370 --> 00:08:28.190
And the gym all the time, like anything,

00:08:28.190 --> 00:08:29.850
anything I do, I do at addictively.

00:08:29.850 --> 00:08:31.080
Anything.

00:08:31.080 --> 00:08:32.323
You know, like, I try
and that's the thing,

00:08:32.323 --> 00:08:34.760
that's the thing that I have is that

00:08:34.760 --> 00:08:37.320
trying to use my brain
to fix all the problems.

00:08:37.320 --> 00:08:40.230
So as soon as I'm clean, that's
one thing that will happen.

00:08:40.230 --> 00:08:41.170
Like I'll go to rehab

00:08:41.170 --> 00:08:42.900
or I'll get like some time clean

00:08:42.900 --> 00:08:45.230
where it's like, okay, I'm gonna be...

00:08:45.230 --> 00:08:46.410
And I switch over.

00:08:46.410 --> 00:08:47.530
And the depression lifts

00:08:47.530 --> 00:08:50.380
and all of a sudden I'm excited
again about being clean.

00:08:50.380 --> 00:08:51.615
But the chance not to be stuck

00:08:51.615 --> 00:08:53.520
and I'll go on like that

00:08:53.520 --> 00:08:55.140
and everything I do, I'll do addictively.

00:08:55.140 --> 00:08:58.330
And I'll try to cram 30
hours into a 24 hour day

00:08:58.330 --> 00:08:59.420
and I'll feel great.

00:08:59.420 --> 00:09:02.880
And everything's like
scheduled and like super anal,

00:09:02.880 --> 00:09:05.270
like, super like, you
know, overboard, obsessive,

00:09:05.270 --> 00:09:07.410
like, with everything that I'm doing.

00:09:07.410 --> 00:09:09.193
I'm trying to be perfect.

00:09:09.193 --> 00:09:10.913
Trying to be perfect.

00:09:13.100 --> 00:09:15.000
I don't know maybe I get burned out on it.

00:09:15.000 --> 00:09:16.184
I don't know.

00:09:16.184 --> 00:09:17.600
- [Mark] Are you perfectionist?

00:09:17.600 --> 00:09:18.433
- Yes.

00:09:18.433 --> 00:09:19.266
- [Mark] You're very
demanding on yourself?

00:09:19.266 --> 00:09:20.535
- Yes.

00:09:20.535 --> 00:09:21.488
Oh, gosh.

00:09:21.488 --> 00:09:22.321
- [Mark] Yeah, I'm sure
there's something there.

00:09:22.321 --> 00:09:23.423
- Very much so.

00:09:23.423 --> 00:09:24.785
Even to the point of, like,

00:09:24.785 --> 00:09:28.230
one thing I have is that I
want everybody to love me.

00:09:28.230 --> 00:09:29.945
I think I mentioned that last video.

00:09:29.945 --> 00:09:30.778
- [Mark] Yeah, you did.

00:09:30.778 --> 00:09:32.850
- I'm always trying to make people laugh.

00:09:32.850 --> 00:09:35.020
Like, I'm always making funny comments

00:09:35.020 --> 00:09:37.531
and I'll say something and I'll be...

00:09:37.531 --> 00:09:40.980
The idea that like, maybe,
like I said something stupid,

00:09:40.980 --> 00:09:42.630
will haunt me, like,
for the rest of the day.

00:09:42.630 --> 00:09:43.463
- [Mark] Right.

00:09:43.463 --> 00:09:45.110
- Like one stupid thing
that nobody cares about,

00:09:45.110 --> 00:09:46.110
nobody would even remember,

00:09:46.110 --> 00:09:47.260
I'm like stewing it.

00:09:47.260 --> 00:09:48.093
Like, Oh, my God.

00:09:48.093 --> 00:09:49.460
- [Mark] Right, I think you said

00:09:49.460 --> 00:09:50.411
you want everyone to love you

00:09:50.411 --> 00:09:51.361
because you don't love yourself.

00:09:51.361 --> 00:09:52.194
- Yeah, yeah.

00:09:52.194 --> 00:09:53.080
So to think I'm brilliant,

00:09:53.080 --> 00:09:55.020
to think I'm, you know, great.

00:09:55.020 --> 00:09:55.910
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:09:55.910 --> 00:09:57.231
- Why people do think that, you know?

00:09:57.231 --> 00:10:00.102
- [Mark] I think
acceptance and forgiveness

00:10:00.102 --> 00:10:03.600
of ourselves most importantly is probably

00:10:03.600 --> 00:10:05.850
at the core of a lot of these problems

00:10:05.850 --> 00:10:07.050
you see on my channel.

00:10:07.050 --> 00:10:08.279
- Yeah, yeah.

00:10:08.279 --> 00:10:09.231
Yeah. True.

00:10:09.231 --> 00:10:10.182
And this is because...

00:10:10.182 --> 00:10:11.017
- [Mark] An outsider would
say, "You're a great guy."

00:10:11.017 --> 00:10:11.850
"You're handsome."

00:10:11.850 --> 00:10:13.172
"You're intelligent."

00:10:13.172 --> 00:10:14.470
"You seem like great in every way."

00:10:14.470 --> 00:10:15.303
- Yeah.

00:10:15.303 --> 00:10:16.136
- [Mark] "Just love yourself."

00:10:16.136 --> 00:10:17.790
"Don't feel the need to be perfect."

00:10:17.790 --> 00:10:20.560
Yeah, that's what someone
would say watching you.

00:10:20.560 --> 00:10:22.487
- Like that same person might say,

00:10:22.487 --> 00:10:25.370
"Yeah and just stop using drugs."

00:10:25.370 --> 00:10:26.203
Like, okay.

00:10:26.203 --> 00:10:27.300
Well, thanks for that.

00:10:28.410 --> 00:10:29.243
I mean that would work.

00:10:29.243 --> 00:10:31.184
Yeah. That would be it.

00:10:31.184 --> 00:10:34.000
That would be, you know, like
that would be a good plan.

00:10:34.000 --> 00:10:35.680
- [Mark] Yeah, I think loving ourselves

00:10:35.680 --> 00:10:37.775
is is the biggest challenge we all have.

00:10:37.775 --> 00:10:38.730
- Yeah.

00:10:38.730 --> 00:10:40.600
- [Mark] Every one of us.

00:10:40.600 --> 00:10:42.030
- It's hard for me to even imagine that,

00:10:42.030 --> 00:10:43.803
to love myself, you know.

00:10:44.950 --> 00:10:46.060
It's hard for me to even imagine.

00:10:46.060 --> 00:10:49.590
It's hard right now for me
to imagine ever doing that.

00:10:49.590 --> 00:10:52.010
- [Mark] And were you
that way since you...

00:10:52.010 --> 00:10:53.847
- I think it's gotten more.

00:10:53.847 --> 00:10:55.570
No, I think it's evolved

00:10:55.570 --> 00:10:56.403
and grown

00:10:56.403 --> 00:10:57.236
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:10:57.236 --> 00:11:00.650
- Incrementally over
the years as I continue

00:11:00.650 --> 00:11:02.200
to not get through this

00:11:02.200 --> 00:11:03.890
because I've been like, try,

00:11:03.890 --> 00:11:05.920
like I've been going do
it, like going to rehab

00:11:05.920 --> 00:11:09.360
and setting my life up
completely around the goal

00:11:09.360 --> 00:11:13.090
of overcoming this since I was 25.

00:11:13.090 --> 00:11:14.700
I'm 42.

00:11:14.700 --> 00:11:17.840
So when I was 25, it's like, okay, great.

00:11:17.840 --> 00:11:18.930
Okay, now I'm clean.

00:11:18.930 --> 00:11:20.740
Maybe I'm clean a year.

00:11:20.740 --> 00:11:22.110
I started believing in God.

00:11:22.110 --> 00:11:23.200
All that was exciting.

00:11:23.200 --> 00:11:24.033
You know, I'm 25.

00:11:24.033 --> 00:11:25.933
I have a whole, my whole
life in front of me.

00:11:25.933 --> 00:11:28.690
Then I got over this crack issue, right?

00:11:28.690 --> 00:11:30.290
And then, no.

00:11:30.290 --> 00:11:32.791
And then, okay, now I'm
26. Yeah, whatever, like

00:11:32.791 --> 00:11:33.624
- [Mark] The older you get,

00:11:33.624 --> 00:11:34.880
the more pressure there is to...

00:11:34.880 --> 00:11:35.850
- And then no.

00:11:35.850 --> 00:11:37.085
And then no, and then no, and then no.

00:11:37.085 --> 00:11:38.233
- [Mark] Time is passing.

00:11:38.233 --> 00:11:39.600
- Right, and at some point along the way,

00:11:39.600 --> 00:11:40.433
like, I get to go to
school and like, you know,

00:11:40.433 --> 00:11:42.000
maybe that's a sign of like, you know,

00:11:42.000 --> 00:11:44.740
kind of getting getting over the hump

00:11:44.740 --> 00:11:46.450
and then no, you know,

00:11:46.450 --> 00:11:47.570
and then moving home

00:11:47.570 --> 00:11:49.043
and starting to work and,

00:11:50.070 --> 00:11:51.820
you know, and then no,

00:11:51.820 --> 00:11:53.970
and just, you know.

00:11:53.970 --> 00:11:55.569
And I work with all these great people

00:11:55.569 --> 00:11:58.020
and just, I know that none
of them do anything like this

00:11:58.020 --> 00:12:01.010
and that sometimes I'll be
at work six months clean,

00:12:01.010 --> 00:12:02.100
not even thinking and all of a sudden,

00:12:02.100 --> 00:12:03.437
I'll just be in the
bathroom and just like,

00:12:03.437 --> 00:12:06.170
"Oh, my god, I can't
believe that I'd do this.

00:12:06.170 --> 00:12:07.470
I did this six months ago."

00:12:07.470 --> 00:12:09.770
- [Mark] No, but it takes
many different forms.

00:12:09.770 --> 00:12:11.941
Yours happens to be a crack addiction.

00:12:11.941 --> 00:12:12.893
- Yeah.

00:12:12.893 --> 00:12:13.845
- [Mark] But there are others

00:12:13.845 --> 00:12:14.678
who have eating

00:12:14.678 --> 00:12:15.750
- Sure.

00:12:15.750 --> 00:12:16.702
- [Mark] Disorders

00:12:16.702 --> 00:12:17.653
- Yeah.

00:12:17.653 --> 00:12:18.603
- [Mark] or gambling

00:12:18.603 --> 00:12:19.553
- Yeah

00:12:19.553 --> 00:12:20.504
- [Mark] or laziness

00:12:20.504 --> 00:12:21.453
- Right.

00:12:21.453 --> 00:12:22.404
- [Mark] or getting too low

00:12:22.404 --> 00:12:23.354
with their relationships' lives.

00:12:23.354 --> 00:12:24.305
- I'm sure.

00:12:24.305 --> 00:12:25.256
Everybody has something.

00:12:25.256 --> 00:12:27.420
I guess I feel like I need to
focus on mine because I'm me.

00:12:27.420 --> 00:12:28.700
And because it's so crazy.

00:12:28.700 --> 00:12:29.533
- [Mark] And you're a perfectionist.

00:12:29.533 --> 00:12:30.366
- And yeah.

00:12:30.366 --> 00:12:31.600
But it's so crazy.

00:12:31.600 --> 00:12:34.353
It's so, you know, it's out there,

00:12:35.205 --> 00:12:37.463
you know, it's way out there.

00:12:43.710 --> 00:12:44.543
- [Mark] Do you think it was something

00:12:44.543 --> 00:12:46.180
about the way you were
raised or your childhood?

00:12:46.180 --> 00:12:47.441
Or do you think...

00:12:47.441 --> 00:12:48.274
- Yeah.

00:12:48.274 --> 00:12:49.107
- [Mark] I keep trying to figure out

00:12:49.107 --> 00:12:50.370
what the cause of it is.

00:12:50.370 --> 00:12:52.260
- I mean, there was that
thing with the molestation,

00:12:52.260 --> 00:12:55.373
I guess I never really thought about.

00:12:56.500 --> 00:12:57.790
But I always had a thing with sex

00:12:57.790 --> 00:12:59.140
like I talked about before.

00:13:02.450 --> 00:13:04.050
I don't know, you know, a lot of it...

00:13:04.050 --> 00:13:05.760
I do know that a lot
of like male behavior,

00:13:05.760 --> 00:13:08.710
like when I'm using is something of a,

00:13:08.710 --> 00:13:10.730
something of a like a chase

00:13:10.730 --> 00:13:15.680
or a trying to recapture
the very beginning

00:13:15.680 --> 00:13:18.260
like when I first discovered all this.

00:13:18.260 --> 00:13:21.940
And I don't want it to
be like that, you know,

00:13:21.940 --> 00:13:24.200
like I like the idea of it back then

00:13:24.200 --> 00:13:27.260
was just so like intriguing.

00:13:27.260 --> 00:13:29.880
And so, like, I wanted to do it so bad

00:13:29.880 --> 00:13:31.575
and it was more like,
I don't know, it was,

00:13:31.575 --> 00:13:34.150
it was more out there back then.

00:13:34.150 --> 00:13:36.130
There was no internet, there
was no cell phones back then.

00:13:36.130 --> 00:13:37.630
So everything was kinda
like on the streets.

00:13:37.630 --> 00:13:38.580
You don't even drive on the streets

00:13:38.580 --> 00:13:40.420
and everything's right there.

00:13:40.420 --> 00:13:41.400
And so.

00:13:41.400 --> 00:13:43.190
- [Mark] Have you talked
to a therapist about this?

00:13:43.190 --> 00:13:45.000
- Off and on over the years, I have.

00:13:45.000 --> 00:13:46.720
I've had great experiences with therapists

00:13:46.720 --> 00:13:50.116
but not obviously
nothing that, you know...

00:13:50.116 --> 00:13:52.713
- [Mark] The more of
these interviews I do,

00:13:53.860 --> 00:13:56.674
we were talking about this
before the cameras started,

00:13:56.674 --> 00:14:00.810
the more I do these, the
more I'm starting to suspect

00:14:00.810 --> 00:14:02.995
or fear that we never really change.

00:14:02.995 --> 00:14:03.880
- Yeah.

00:14:03.880 --> 00:14:06.600
- [Mark] We might improve
a little bit incrementally.

00:14:06.600 --> 00:14:07.433
- Yeah.

00:14:07.433 --> 00:14:08.791
- [Mark] If we really work hard at it

00:14:08.791 --> 00:14:11.020
and have a lot of courage
and forgive ourselves

00:14:11.020 --> 00:14:12.900
and all the things that we've mentioned.

00:14:12.900 --> 00:14:14.900
But we never really just

00:14:14.900 --> 00:14:16.390
all of a sudden become perfectly healthy

00:14:16.390 --> 00:14:18.200
and functioning, fully functional.

00:14:18.200 --> 00:14:20.866
- I think people do more
than maybe you see down here,

00:14:20.866 --> 00:14:22.920
now that I'm thinking
about it a little more,

00:14:22.920 --> 00:14:24.860
and I go to AAA meetings and NA meetings.

00:14:24.860 --> 00:14:27.700
And there's definitely
people there that are,

00:14:27.700 --> 00:14:29.372
even though maybe I
didn't know them before,

00:14:29.372 --> 00:14:31.040
you can just tell.

00:14:31.040 --> 00:14:31.970
Like the way they are.

00:14:31.970 --> 00:14:33.450
- [Mark] They've
straighten their lives out.

00:14:33.450 --> 00:14:34.700
- They're just different people.

00:14:34.700 --> 00:14:36.309
They're different people altogether.

00:14:36.309 --> 00:14:38.877
The way they look at
the world is different.

00:14:38.877 --> 00:14:40.630
- [Mark] Yeah, I think
that's what's needed.

00:14:40.630 --> 00:14:43.280
- Yeah, and I feel like
maybe I've tasted that

00:14:43.280 --> 00:14:45.395
a little bit here and there, you know,

00:14:45.395 --> 00:14:48.400
it's like looking at the
world from the angle of,

00:14:48.400 --> 00:14:51.060
okay, God is real, first of all.

00:14:51.060 --> 00:14:53.040
So like, whatever happens,

00:14:53.040 --> 00:14:54.580
I don't have to even worry about it.

00:14:54.580 --> 00:14:56.440
Like all this that I
have, I could accept it

00:14:56.440 --> 00:14:58.750
and then I won't worry about
it because God is real.

00:14:58.750 --> 00:15:00.980
And then going about life

00:15:00.980 --> 00:15:04.470
with the number one priority
being to help somebody else.

00:15:04.470 --> 00:15:05.422
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:15:05.422 --> 00:15:06.255
- There's people that, like, do that

00:15:06.255 --> 00:15:10.340
as a practice, as a way of life.

00:15:10.340 --> 00:15:13.530
And that's sort of the
goal of those programs

00:15:13.530 --> 00:15:15.820
is to build that way of life.

00:15:15.820 --> 00:15:17.760
To do little things day by day

00:15:17.760 --> 00:15:20.060
and do sort of like work on like,

00:15:20.060 --> 00:15:21.440
going back into your own life

00:15:21.440 --> 00:15:22.630
and seeing where some of the stuff

00:15:22.630 --> 00:15:24.423
that came up through some writing.

00:15:26.050 --> 00:15:27.610
And then you're able to like launch out

00:15:27.610 --> 00:15:30.557
and be out there helping
other people like me.

00:15:30.557 --> 00:15:32.910
And I know dudes like this that are very,

00:15:32.910 --> 00:15:34.120
like, very much like that.

00:15:34.120 --> 00:15:35.040
They're very like

00:15:36.500 --> 00:15:38.177
attractive, you know.

00:15:38.177 --> 00:15:41.092
Those are like the guys
that I want to be like.

00:15:41.092 --> 00:15:41.925
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:15:41.925 --> 00:15:42.758
- I like that in my life.

00:15:42.758 --> 00:15:44.049
- [Mark] And I know that people do change.

00:15:44.049 --> 00:15:44.882
- Yeah.

00:15:44.882 --> 00:15:45.790
- [Mark] I've known them in my life.

00:15:45.790 --> 00:15:46.902
- Yeah.

00:15:46.902 --> 00:15:47.853
- [Mark] People that have really

00:15:47.853 --> 00:15:48.686
made that huge transformation.

00:15:48.686 --> 00:15:51.482
- Yeah, but it has to be sort
of like, along those lines.

00:15:51.482 --> 00:15:53.150
I think you might be right.

00:15:53.150 --> 00:15:54.950
Like, people like me,

00:15:54.950 --> 00:15:56.733
we don't just change ourselves.

00:15:56.733 --> 00:15:58.420
I mean, if we don't do anything,

00:15:58.420 --> 00:16:01.049
it's definitely, nothing's
gonna change, you know.

00:16:01.049 --> 00:16:02.770
For me even doing a lot,
it seems like nothing.

00:16:02.770 --> 00:16:03.830
- [Mark] And for some
people, it's religion

00:16:03.830 --> 00:16:05.852
and for other people, it's like exercise

00:16:05.852 --> 00:16:07.880
or something extreme.

00:16:07.880 --> 00:16:08.713
- Yeah.

00:16:08.713 --> 00:16:10.760
But, to me, I think that
helping others' peace

00:16:10.760 --> 00:16:12.570
is a huge part of it.

00:16:12.570 --> 00:16:13.403
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:16:13.403 --> 00:16:14.680
- Like not living for
myself 'cause that's...

00:16:14.680 --> 00:16:17.100
At the core of this thing is very selfish.

00:16:17.100 --> 00:16:20.690
Like, drug addiction is a selfish thing.

00:16:20.690 --> 00:16:21.683
It just is.

00:16:23.797 --> 00:16:26.530
And so like the antidote to selfishness

00:16:26.530 --> 00:16:28.510
is to like not think of yourself at all.

00:16:28.510 --> 00:16:30.167
To be like, "What can I
do for the next person?"

00:16:30.167 --> 00:16:31.474
"How can I help this person."

00:16:31.474 --> 00:16:33.023
You know, so...

00:16:33.023 --> 00:16:34.340
- [Mark] And if that's the case,

00:16:34.340 --> 00:16:37.608
do you think it's courage

00:16:37.608 --> 00:16:41.850
to not be selfish or to do things

00:16:41.850 --> 00:16:44.040
that you've never done before
or something like that?

00:16:44.040 --> 00:16:46.100
To me, courage is a big part of all this.

00:16:46.100 --> 00:16:48.690
- I mean, courage, I think
courage comes along the way.

00:16:48.690 --> 00:16:49.523
- [Mark] It's not

00:16:49.523 --> 00:16:52.072
determination and discipline.

00:16:52.072 --> 00:16:54.510
- A little bit, a little
bit of it is discipline.

00:16:54.510 --> 00:16:56.120
Not so much discipline not to use,

00:16:56.120 --> 00:16:58.160
but discipline to do the right thing.

00:16:58.160 --> 00:17:00.790
Discipline to, you know,
get up in the morning

00:17:00.790 --> 00:17:02.567
and like sort of start the day,

00:17:02.567 --> 00:17:04.350
thinking a lot, thinking about it

00:17:04.350 --> 00:17:06.010
in those sort of the natural way.

00:17:06.010 --> 00:17:06.843
- [Mark] Yeah, no, I mean...

00:17:06.843 --> 00:17:07.766
- What can I do today?

00:17:07.766 --> 00:17:09.386
How can I help somebody else today?

00:17:09.386 --> 00:17:10.797
- [Mark] Certainly, discipline, support.

00:17:10.797 --> 00:17:13.073
- Yeah, and just to be committed to that.

00:17:13.073 --> 00:17:16.810
And I mean, the times I've had a few like,

00:17:16.810 --> 00:17:20.340
opportunities to help
people like even directly

00:17:20.340 --> 00:17:23.650
through sponsoring in the 12
steps or that sort of thing

00:17:23.650 --> 00:17:25.185
or just even talking about it.

00:17:25.185 --> 00:17:27.770
Whenever I do, I feel better.

00:17:27.770 --> 00:17:30.480
Like whenever I do, I
feel like, I feel great.

00:17:30.480 --> 00:17:31.730
Like it's a good feeling.

00:17:31.730 --> 00:17:33.110
And I wasn't even seeking that feeling,

00:17:33.110 --> 00:17:35.640
I was just trying to
help the other person.

00:17:35.640 --> 00:17:37.220
So,

00:17:37.220 --> 00:17:38.053
that's a thing,

00:17:38.053 --> 00:17:40.960
but there is always the big question

00:17:40.960 --> 00:17:43.132
like why isn't it sticking?

00:17:43.132 --> 00:17:44.085
- [Mark] That's where I'm suspicious.

00:17:44.085 --> 00:17:46.170
That maybe courage is the answer.

00:17:46.170 --> 00:17:48.260
Whereas, if you just
started doing some helping

00:17:48.260 --> 00:17:49.411
- [Patrick] Mm-hmm.

00:17:49.411 --> 00:17:50.500
- [Mark] And maybe dug in deeper

00:17:50.500 --> 00:17:52.554
and even helped further on a deeper level

00:17:52.554 --> 00:17:53.505
- [Patrick] Mm-hmm.

00:17:53.505 --> 00:17:55.240
- [Mark] Really committed to it.

00:17:55.240 --> 00:17:56.073
- [Patrick] Yeah.

00:17:56.073 --> 00:17:57.680
- [Mark] Then your self
perception would change so...

00:17:57.680 --> 00:17:59.460
- [Patrick] It could be.

00:17:59.460 --> 00:18:00.730
- [Mark] So deeply, so profoundly

00:18:00.730 --> 00:18:02.840
that you would no longer

00:18:04.810 --> 00:18:06.030
feel any shame.

00:18:06.030 --> 00:18:07.080
- [Patrick] Yeah.

00:18:07.080 --> 00:18:08.030
- [Mark] If the shame would disappear.

00:18:08.030 --> 00:18:11.521
- [Mark] Shame's a big,
shame's a huge factor.

00:18:11.521 --> 00:18:13.130
- [Patrick] Oh, yeah. Crippling.

00:18:13.130 --> 00:18:13.963
- [Mark] I mean, if you were

00:18:13.963 --> 00:18:15.400
to consistently do things

00:18:16.570 --> 00:18:17.870
that would make it impossible for you

00:18:17.870 --> 00:18:20.590
to see yourself as anything other than

00:18:20.590 --> 00:18:24.870
altruistic and kind and a good person

00:18:24.870 --> 00:18:26.460
where you're helping others relentlessly,

00:18:26.460 --> 00:18:29.483
wouldn't that impact your
self-worth significantly?

00:18:30.480 --> 00:18:32.720
- [Patrick] Yeah, I think that's true.

00:18:32.720 --> 00:18:35.270
Maybe I just haven't gotten
deep enough into it yet.

00:18:35.270 --> 00:18:36.720
Well, maybe like,

00:18:36.720 --> 00:18:39.710
if I could get past
six months, nine months

00:18:39.710 --> 00:18:42.160
without a relapse happening
and continue on the path

00:18:42.160 --> 00:18:43.040
that I've been on, you know?

00:18:43.040 --> 00:18:44.180
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:18:44.180 --> 00:18:45.310
Because whether it's

00:18:47.060 --> 00:18:50.440
drug addiction or sex work or whatever,

00:18:50.440 --> 00:18:53.240
whatever your vice is, it creates shame.

00:18:53.240 --> 00:18:54.073
- [Patrick] Yes.

00:18:54.073 --> 00:18:54.906
- [Mark] If you can do something

00:18:54.906 --> 00:18:56.680
that really erases that shame

00:18:56.680 --> 00:18:59.167
and usually helping another
is a great way to do that

00:18:59.167 --> 00:19:00.612
but what better way, right?

00:19:00.612 --> 00:19:01.445
- [Patrick] Right.

00:19:01.445 --> 00:19:02.278
- [Mark] Then all of a sudden,

00:19:02.278 --> 00:19:03.111
your shame disappears.

00:19:03.111 --> 00:19:04.431
And without the shame, then,

00:19:04.431 --> 00:19:08.190
that was your number one
factor why you're doing

00:19:08.190 --> 00:19:09.930
this self-destructive
stuff in the first place.

00:19:09.930 --> 00:19:11.210
- [Patrick] Yeah.

00:19:11.210 --> 00:19:13.500
- [Mark] So, you're thinking of rehab now?

00:19:13.500 --> 00:19:14.679
- Yeah. That's what I,

00:19:14.679 --> 00:19:15.512
That's what I should do.

00:19:15.512 --> 00:19:17.400
That's what, you know, that's...

00:19:17.400 --> 00:19:19.697
the clear thing that I should do.

00:19:19.697 --> 00:19:22.259
I'm considering going to the East coast

00:19:22.259 --> 00:19:24.173
where I have some friends.

00:19:25.039 --> 00:19:28.633
Or probably here, I haven't decided where.

00:19:29.860 --> 00:19:30.780
And just try again.

00:19:30.780 --> 00:19:32.082
I guess what my mom says is, "Try again.

00:19:32.082 --> 00:19:34.400
What can you do except try again?"

00:19:34.400 --> 00:19:37.080
And it's like all the other options,

00:19:37.080 --> 00:19:39.700
you know, I don't know, would be like...

00:19:39.700 --> 00:19:40.640
Die?

00:19:40.640 --> 00:19:41.603
Get homeless?

00:19:44.160 --> 00:19:44.993
I've never really been homeless.

00:19:44.993 --> 00:19:46.900
I don't know if I could hang on that.

00:19:46.900 --> 00:19:47.733
And

00:19:47.733 --> 00:19:49.160
- [Mark] Yeah, I think the helping thing

00:19:49.160 --> 00:19:50.050
is probably something that...

00:19:50.050 --> 00:19:51.390
- It's back to that.

00:19:51.390 --> 00:19:54.100
Yeah. I mean, it's pitiful.

00:19:54.100 --> 00:19:56.000
Like this whole thing is just pitiful.

00:19:58.507 --> 00:19:59.340
I'm getting old.

00:20:00.350 --> 00:20:01.670
I don't really care, you know,

00:20:01.670 --> 00:20:02.850
I was talking to my dad about this, too.

00:20:02.850 --> 00:20:06.551
Like, I don't really care, like,

00:20:06.551 --> 00:20:09.770
prestige or position or money

00:20:09.770 --> 00:20:12.970
has never really been like the motivator,

00:20:12.970 --> 00:20:15.790
like the driving factor for
me to be happy or content.

00:20:15.790 --> 00:20:18.890
Like I've been in
long-term rehab situations

00:20:18.890 --> 00:20:21.250
where I've had like pretty much no money.

00:20:21.250 --> 00:20:22.700
And I was totally happy.

00:20:22.700 --> 00:20:26.130
I was just as happy as I'll
be here working, you know.

00:20:26.130 --> 00:20:29.240
Every, any situation that I ever am in.

00:20:29.240 --> 00:20:33.370
if I'm clean and being
productive, that I'm content.

00:20:33.370 --> 00:20:36.400
And I, so, I don't know, you know.

00:20:36.400 --> 00:20:38.040
I don't know, like I mentioned

00:20:38.040 --> 00:20:39.720
teen challenge last time.

00:20:39.720 --> 00:20:41.790
Teen challenge is where I
had the longest, you know,

00:20:41.790 --> 00:20:44.060
the most, probably highest percentage

00:20:44.060 --> 00:20:46.740
of days clean in a stretch.

00:20:46.740 --> 00:20:48.570
But a lot of that was
because I was living there.

00:20:48.570 --> 00:20:52.000
You like live there and help
work there with the students

00:20:52.000 --> 00:20:53.347
- [Mark] That you were helping.

00:20:53.347 --> 00:20:54.180
- But maybe that's what it...

00:20:54.180 --> 00:20:55.780
Maybe I'm just not cut out for it.

00:20:55.780 --> 00:20:57.060
Maybe I need to go somewhere like that

00:20:57.060 --> 00:20:58.147
and just stay for the rest of my life.

00:20:58.147 --> 00:20:59.900
And people do that.

00:20:59.900 --> 00:21:01.150
Wouldn't be the end of the world.

00:21:01.150 --> 00:21:02.902
And I would be helping people.

00:21:02.902 --> 00:21:03.977
I would probably be happy.

00:21:03.977 --> 00:21:05.840
But I wouldn't have any
money, but who cares?

00:21:05.840 --> 00:21:06.673
You know?

00:21:06.673 --> 00:21:07.908
- [Mark] Wow.

00:21:07.908 --> 00:21:09.340
Yeah, the older I get, the more I think

00:21:09.340 --> 00:21:12.967
that there are alternative paths in life

00:21:12.967 --> 00:21:14.040
- Yeah.

00:21:14.040 --> 00:21:15.870
- [Mark] That can lead to
happiness and fulfillment.

00:21:15.870 --> 00:21:16.950
- Yeah.

00:21:16.950 --> 00:21:18.330
- [Mark] Then what society

00:21:18.330 --> 00:21:19.163
- Right.

00:21:19.163 --> 00:21:20.262
- [Mark] says you're supposed to do.

00:21:20.262 --> 00:21:22.733
- Yeah, and I'll probably be...

00:21:22.733 --> 00:21:25.370
I would be very very helpful to people

00:21:25.370 --> 00:21:26.840
- [Mark] I'm sure you will.

00:21:26.840 --> 00:21:28.190
- If I get my act together.

00:21:31.256 --> 00:21:34.971
- [Mark] I can totally
see you doing great things

00:21:34.971 --> 00:21:37.180
for yourself and for others.

00:21:37.180 --> 00:21:38.013
- Yeah.

00:21:38.013 --> 00:21:38.846
- [Mark] Very clearly.

00:21:38.846 --> 00:21:39.679
- Yeah.

00:21:41.367 --> 00:21:43.248
- [Mark] But we all
need to get out of this

00:21:43.248 --> 00:21:44.081
- Yeah.

00:21:44.081 --> 00:21:44.914
- [Mark] quick sand that you're in here.

00:21:44.914 --> 00:21:45.747
- Yeah.

00:21:46.610 --> 00:21:47.660
Yeah, now's the time.

00:21:49.980 --> 00:21:50.980
- [Mark] Absolutely.

00:21:51.880 --> 00:21:53.220
Well, Patrick, I wish you the best of luck

00:21:53.220 --> 00:21:54.990
with whatever you do.

00:21:54.990 --> 00:21:55.823
- Thanks, Mark.

00:21:55.823 --> 00:21:58.190
- [Mark] And maybe we'll
do this again one day.

00:21:58.190 --> 00:22:00.260
- Yeah, let's do it again,
you know, down the road

00:22:00.260 --> 00:22:02.280
and see the difference, you know,

00:22:02.280 --> 00:22:03.300
there's definitely a difference.

00:22:03.300 --> 00:22:04.570
You'll see a difference between me.

00:22:04.570 --> 00:22:06.710
I'm not high compared to last time

00:22:06.710 --> 00:22:10.580
but if you catch me three months clean,

00:22:10.580 --> 00:22:12.187
you'll see the difference
between this and that for sure.

00:22:12.187 --> 00:22:13.800
- [Mark] Oh, I'd love to see you again.

00:22:13.800 --> 00:22:15.000
That'd be great.

00:22:15.000 --> 00:22:15.833
- All right.

00:22:15.833 --> 00:22:16.673
- [Mark] All right.

00:22:16.673 --> 00:22:18.340
Thank you very much.

